1790667836.037	
1790667836.037	The most significant precursor technique that eventually informed the printing revolution was **woodblock printing (xylography)**. This method arose independently in East Asia, particularly in China and Korea. Woodblock printing involved carving an entire page of text and images onto a single block of wood, which was then inked and pressed onto paper or fabric.
